DESCRIPTION:Topic: The New Civic Architects: Rise of the Entrepreneurial S
 ocial Club\n\nIn an increasingly isolated\, digital\, and fragmented econo
 my\, people have gotten very entrepreneurial about community building. Hou
 se parties\, "going to the bar"\, and other unstructured activities have f
 allen by the wayside in favour of highly structured\, curated\, sometimes-
 professionally-useful\, often ticketed\, community event series -- especia
 lly for Gen Z.\n\nWhile critics worry about the commercialization of frien
 dship\, this talk explores what is actually driving this boom\, and explor
 es why a small army of entrepreneurial community builders might just be th
 e civic architects we need to absorb the economic shockwaves of the next d
 ecade.\n\n‎\n\nSpeaker: Joss Murphy (in-person)\n\nJoss is the cofounder
  and CEO of Wygo\, where she builds tools for entrepreneurial community ev
 ent organizers to scale their businesses and organizations sustainably.\n\
 nShe's one of the founding team members of Socratica (a global network of 
 in-person creative communities that grew to over 100 hosts across 30+ citi
 es) and a Systems Design Engineering graduate from the University of Water
 loo.\n\n‎\n\nAgenda:\n\n7:00-7:20 Welcome and Introductions\n\n7:20-7:50
  Presentation and Q\\&A/discussion\n\n7:50-9:00 Breakout groups\n\n‎\n\n
 Code of Conduct: https://civictech.ca/about-us\n\n‎\n\nCheck in with us 
 on the Civic Tech Toronto Slack: https://link.civictech.ca/chat\n\n‎\n\n
 About Us:\n\nOur weekly civic meetups bring together Torontonians (designe
 rs\, coders\, urban planners\, government staff\, mappers\, policy-makers\
 , students\, communications strategists\, community organizers\, and more)
  who share an interest in making Toronto more responsive\, prosperous\, su
 stainable\, and equitable through design\, tech\, and data.\n\nCome and be
  part of it!\n\nFor more info: https://civictech.ca\n\n\\--\n\nSuggest a S
 peaker:&#x20\;\n\nInterested in speaking at a future event\, or know someo
 ne who'd be a great speaker? We'd love to hear from you: https://link.civi
 ctech.ca/speaker-suggestions\n\nSuggest a Venue:&#x20\;\n\nHave a space th
 at could host up to 80 civic-minded folks for an evening? Consider recomme
 nding your venue: https://link.civictech.ca/venue-suggestions\n
